---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import CaseStudySection from "../../components/CaseStudySection.astro";

// Rebuilt from Figma "eduseek casestudy" frame (node 750:6173)
// https://www.figma.com/design/2nYhgPKrVIuNd9J4G02Mae/ai-app?node-id=750-6173
// GIF sections use local files in public/images/work/eduseek/ (pulled from the
// frame's animated fills via rawImages, not Figma's flattened static export).

const meta = [
	{ label: "Timeline", value: "Nov 2025 - Feb 2026" },
	{ label: "Role", value: "UX Designer" },
	{ label: "Tools", value: "Figma, Magic Patterns" },
	{ label: "Deliverables", value: "Calendar Navigation, Key Insights Feature, Mobile Adaptation" },
];

const panel =
	"flex w-full flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4 rounded-[4px] bg-[#1e1e1e] px-4 py-8";
const caption = "max-w-[480px] text-center font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#e8e7e3]";
---

<CaseStudyLayout
	title="Eduseek.AI"
	heroSrc="/images/work/eduseek/hero.png"
	heroAlt="Eduseek.AI session replay dashboard"
	meta={meta}
>
	<CaseStudySection eyebrow="Outcome" heading="From an 8-click bottleneck to a 3-click habit">
		<div class={panel}>
			<img
				src="/images/work/eduseek/Figma_7ake3cWfCV.gif"
				alt="Calendar navigation with Year, Month, and Week toggle"
				class="w-full max-w-[353px] rounded-[4px]"
			/>
			<img
				src="/images/work/eduseek/Figma_VJ9ajLfiwp.gif"
				alt="Key Insights card with color-coded progress meters"
				class="w-full max-w-[326px] rounded-[4px]"
			/>
		</div>
		<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#1a1a1a]">
			Sixteen weeks of working directly with the CEO turned a UI refresh request into a full
			diagnostic of how teachers actually use the product. Testing confirmed calendar navigation
			dropped from 8 clicks to 3. The Key Insights feature I designed shipped as the solution the
			CEO specifically flagged for surfacing actionable data at no added AI generation cost. The
			mobile rebuild took a session replay experience from unusable to fully functional on phones
			and tablets. What started as a UI refresh became the redesign that reshaped how 17 schools
			review student progress.
		</p>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection eyebrow="Context" heading="The platform">
		<div class="flex items-center justify-center rounded-[4px] bg-[#1e1e1e] p-2">
			<img
				src="/images/work/eduseek/context.png"
				alt="Eduseek.AI platform dashboard overview"
				class="aspect-[960/479] w-full rounded-[4px] object-contain"
			/>
		</div>
		<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#1a1a1a]">
			EduSeek.AI is a B2B EdTech startup building AI tutoring tools for schools and teachers.
			Their session replay system lets teachers review AI tutoring conversations and student
			interactions. I joined as the sole designer for 16 weeks, working directly with the CEO.
		</p>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection eyebrow="Problem" heading="The data existed, but teachers couldn't use it">
		<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#1a1a1a]">
			Teachers were spending hours reviewing tutoring sessions, but the interface made it nearly
			impossible to find what they needed. Navigation took 8+ clicks to reach a single
			conversation, mastery scores showed up with no context behind them, and the whole system
			only worked on desktop. The data existed. The experience to act on it didn't.
		</p>
		<div class="flex w-full flex-col items-center gap-8 rounded-[4px] bg-[#1e1e1e] px-4 py-8">
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
				<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base font-bold text-[#e8e7e3]">Pain Point 1</p>
				<img
					src="/images/work/eduseek/firefox_5domEKwecf.gif"
					alt="Old calendar navigation requiring many clicks to reach a session"
					class="w-full max-w-[628px] rounded-[4px]"
				/>
				<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#e8e7e3]">Teachers were clicking blind</p>
				<p class={caption}>
					Teachers were spending 8+ clicks to reach past sessions, and the existing system would
					jump straight to the end of the week on click, making it nearly impossible to find a
					specific conversation.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
				<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base font-bold text-[#e8e7e3]">Pain Point 2</p>
				<img
					src="/images/work/eduseek/firefox_DwvTlVIXaS.gif"
					alt="Mastery score shown without supporting context"
					class="w-full max-w-[228px] rounded-[4px]"
				/>
				<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#e8e7e3]">Numbers with no story behind them</p>
				<p class={caption}>
					A mastery score told teachers nothing about where a student actually struggled.
					Teachers were staring at numbers with no context to act on.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection eyebrow="Design Decisions" heading="From 8 clicks to 3, with navigation that stays put">
		<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#1a1a1a]">
			I tried keeping the existing single-scroll week list and just restyling it, since that was
			the original ask. But testing showed the design still had teachers clicking 8+ times, and
			the jump-to-end-of-week behavior meant one wrong click cost a full re-navigation.
		</p>
		<div class="flex w-full flex-col items-center gap-8 rounded-[4px] bg-[#1e1e1e] px-4 py-8">
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
				<img
					src="/images/work/eduseek/Figma_7ake3cWfCV.gif"
					alt="Year, Month, and Week toggle navigation next to the restyled calendar"
					class="w-full max-w-[353px] rounded-[4px]"
				/>
				<p class={caption}>
					Fix: built a Year / Month / Week toggle so any session was reachable in 2-3 clicks, with
					navigation that holds its position instead of resetting.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
				<img
					src="/images/work/eduseek/design-decision-1-process.png"
					alt="Component states for the calendar navigation iterated in Magic Patterns"
					class="w-full max-w-[736px] rounded-[4px]"
				/>
				<p class={caption}>
					Process: iterated on component states in Magic Patterns before finalizing in Figma, so
					designs were production-ready from the start.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection eyebrow="Design Decisions" heading="Surfacing the story behind the score">
		<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#1a1a1a]">
			I designed a Key Insights feature that auto-summarizes the critical learning moments from
			each AI conversation at no additional generation cost, paired with color-coded progress
			meters so teachers can read comprehension at a glance and act on it, not just observe it.
		</p>
		<div class={panel}>
			<img
				src="/images/work/eduseek/Figma_VJ9ajLfiwp.gif"
				alt="Key Insights summary card and color-coded progress meters"
				class="w-full max-w-[265px] rounded-[4px]"
			/>
			<img
				src="/images/work/eduseek/Figma_MOmgMZSepS.gif"
				alt="Key Insights summary card and color-coded progress meters, detail view"
				class="w-full max-w-[265px] rounded-[4px]"
			/>
		</div>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection eyebrow="Design Decisions" heading="Extending access beyond the classroom">
		<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#1a1a1a]">
			Teachers review student progress on the go, not just at their desks, but the existing mobile
			interface made session replay nearly unusable. I rebuilt the mobile experience to preserve
			full functionality across phones and tablets, matching the desktop redesign instead of
			trailing behind it.
		</p>
		<div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-center gap-8 rounded-[4px] bg-[#1e1e1e] px-4 py-8">
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
				<img
					src="/images/work/eduseek/mobile-before.png"
					alt="Original mobile session replay view with overlapping components"
					class="w-full max-w-[322px] rounded-[4px]"
				/>
				<p class={caption}>Original mobile view with break due to components not adjusting.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
				<img
					src="/images/work/eduseek/mobile-after.png"
					alt="Redesigned mobile session replay view adapted for phone screens"
					class="w-full max-w-[280px] rounded-[4px]"
				/>
				<p class={caption}>
					Redesigned mobile components to match the new UI and work properly at mobile screen
					sizes.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection eyebrow="Outcome" heading="What I learned">
		<div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
			<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#1a1a1a]">
				What started as a UI redesign became a focused diagnostic. Over 16 weeks working directly
				with the CEO, I solved the core friction points teachers were actually hitting, not just
				the ones in the original brief.
			</p>
			<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#1a1a1a]">
				Calendar navigation dropped from 8 clicks to 3. Key Insights shipped as the solution the
				CEO flagged for surfacing actionable data at no added AI cost. The component library grew
				from 14 to 17, making handoff to dev straightforward.
			</p>
		</div>
	</CaseStudySection>

	<CaseStudySection eyebrow="Try it" heading="INTERACTIVE PROTOTYPE">
		<p class="font-space-grotesk text-base text-[#1a1a1a]">
			Explore the session replay dashboard prototype below, built in Magic Patterns to test the
			calendar navigation and Key Insights feature before handoff to engineering.
		</p>
		<iframe
			src="https://project-session-replay-dashboard-ui-896.magicpatterns.app"
			width="100%"
			height="700"
			style="border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #d4d2cc;"
			title="Eduseek.AI interactive prototype"></iframe>
	</CaseStudySection>
</CaseStudyLayout>
